        "title": "Design what visitors see",
        "body": "Use another typed node for a concrete part of that idea. It has its own fields and a shared presentation, supplied by a class.",
        "role": "part",
        "check": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "how-it-works-edges-note",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "CONNECT · Relations are stored",
      "position": {
        "x": -390,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 1050,
      "height": 390,
      "style": {
        "background": "#213f60",
        "color": "#f7faff",
        "borderColor": "#8fb5df",
        "borderRadius": 17
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "how-it-works",
          "nodeId": "how-it-works-edges-note"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style=\"container-type:inline-size;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;background:#213f60;color:#fff;border:3px solid #8fb5df;border-radius:4cqw;padding:4.5cqw;font-family:system-ui\"><div style=\"font:800 2.7cqw/1.15 system-ui;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#f5c542\">02 / CONNECT</div><h2 style=\"font:650 6.1cqw/1.09 Georgia,serif;margin:2.4cqw 0 1.8cqw\">An edge is a fact.</h2><p style=\"font:470 3.8cqw/1.36 system-ui;margin:0;color:#e6effc\">A relationship is stored in the graph, not merely drawn on a screen. An AI can read it, follow it, or change it.</p></div>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "how-it-works-class-note",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "REUSE · Classes describe nodes",
      "position": {
        "x": 900,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 1050,
      "height": 390,
      "style": {
        "background": "#3c2e59",
        "color": "#f7faff",
        "borderColor": "#b2a0db",
        "borderRadius": 17
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "how-it-works",
          "nodeId": "how-it-works-class-note"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style=\"container-type:inline-size;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;background:#3c2e59;color:#fff;border:3px solid #b2a0db;border-radius:4cqw;padding:4.5cqw;font-family:system-ui\"><div style=\"font:800 2.7cqw/1.15 system-ui;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#f5c542\">03 / REUSE</div><h2 style=\"font:650 6.1cqw/1.09 Georgia,serif;margin:2.4cqw 0 1.8cqw\">Build once. Borrow.</h2><p style=\"font:470 3.8cqw/1.36 system-ui;margin:0;color:#e6effc\">These Idea and Point nodes are instances of reusable classes. Their structure and presentation don't need to be invented again.</p></div>"
        }
      }
    },
